      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Don't worry, I'm here to help you navigate the complexities of travel visas. You're not alone in feeling overwhelmed, but I'll break it down for you in a way that's easy to understand. \n\nFirst, let's start with the basics: Singapore, Vietnam, and Thailand all have their own unique visa requirements, but I'll give you a general checklist to get you started. \n\nFor Singapore, you'll need to check if your group members have a valid visa on arrival (VOA) or an Electronic Travel Authorization (SG Arrival Card). If you're flying into Singapore, you can opt for the VOA, which is usually processed quickly. However, if you're taking a layover, you might need to check with the airline for their specific requirements.\n\nVietnam, on the other hand, has a bit more complexity. You'll need to determine if your group members need a visa on arrival (VOA) or an e-visa. If you're flying into Vietnam, the VOA is usually the way to go, but if you're taking a layover, you'll need to check with the airline and the Vietnamese embassy or consulate for more information.\n\nThailand has a bit of a mix of both. If",
